{"term":"whistle","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f76738e681a44136fd","definition":"A device designed to be placed in the mouth and blown, or driven by steam or some other mechanism, to make a whistling sound.","example":"A lovely crisp exhaust: a feeling of almost unlimited power combined with complete freedom of running: and, to crown it all, a most melodious and wholly American chime whistle—these were my immediate impressions as we stormed rapidly out of Göttingen, intent on winning back some of the lost time.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1865cea4e106f0522f","definition":"An act of whistling.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:163c6633465375bc5f","definition":"A shrill, high-pitched sound made by whistling.","example":"We expressed our readiness, and in ten minutes were in the station wagon, rolling rapidly down the long drive, for it was then after nine.[…]As we reached the lodge we heard the whistle, and we backed up against one side of the platform as the train pulled up at the other.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:05894ec10ac56d8c02","definition":"Any high-pitched sound similar to the sound made by whistling.","example":"the whistle of the wind in the trees","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c5ef449379d13856ff","definition":"A suit (from whistle and flute).","example":"We soldiers changed into our No.1 dress uniforms, Sid into his best whistle and we set off for the church.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Cockney, slang","register":"Cockney, countable, slang, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:28a481103d0ebb52a3","definition":"The mouth and throat; so called as being the organs of whistling.","example":"Let's […] drink the other cup to wet our whistles.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d196c3725b6f1970f3","definition":"To make a shrill, high-pitched sound by forcing air through the mouth. To produce a whistling sound, restrictions to the flow of air are created using the teeth, tongue and lips.","example":"Never whistle at a funeral.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c370d9d4e08c9c7a06","definition":"To make a similar sound by forcing air through a musical instrument or a pipe etc.","example":"The steam train whistled as it passed by.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3740590012e8fec0c2","definition":"To move in such a way as to create a whistling sound.","example":"A bullet whistled past.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ef2af450af9430b1ea","definition":"To send, signal, or call by a whistle.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f6ed325c3d4f86cc1","definition":"To request admission to Opus Dei, a Roman Catholic organization.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"intransitive, slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈwɪs(ə)l/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/56/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-whistle.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-whistle.wav.mp3"},"wordFamily":[]}